1. Copyright

The learning platform – source code, learning content (texts, exercises, quiz questions, games),
graphics and documentation – is protected by copyright. All rights remain with the author unless
these terms expressly permit otherwise. The fact that the source code is publicly visible does not
make this project open-source software; no open-source licence is granted.

2. Permitted use

The online version of the learning platform operated by the author may be used within its features;
the terms and conditions and the privacy policy published there apply in addition. The source code
may be viewed on GitHub.

3. Not permitted

Beyond the use permitted under section 2, you may not, without the author's prior consent (text
form, e.g. e-mail, suffices):

   a) reproduce, modify or translate (including compile) the source code, program files or content
      in whole or in part, incorporate them into other software or works, or run your own instances
      of them;
   b) distribute, publish, sell or rent out the project or parts of it, or pass it off as your own
      work;
   c) remove or alter copyright, licence or trademark notices.

Linking to the repository or the official download page is expressly permitted. Uses permitted by
law (in particular sections 44a et seq., 69d and 69e of the German Copyright Act) and viewing and
forking the repository on GitHub under the GitHub Terms of Service remain unaffected.

4. Third-party components

assets/vendor/ contains Bootstrap 5.3.0, Bootstrap Icons 1.10.0, Chart.js 4.4.1, SortableJS 1.15.0
and TinyMCE 6.8.5 (each under the MIT licence) with the German TinyMCE translation from
tinymce-i18n; assets/fonts/ contains the Inter typeface (SIL Open Font License 1.1). The licence
texts are stored alongside them. They are governed exclusively by their own licences; these terms do
not restrict the rights granted by those licences.

5. Liability and warranty

The software is provided free of charge. The author is therefore liable only for intent and gross
negligence and for fraudulently concealed defects (sections 521, 523, 524 German Civil Code).
Liability under the German Product Liability Act and any other mandatory statutory liability remain
unaffected.

No warranty is given that the learning platform works without errors or is fit for a particular
purpose. There is no entitlement to bug fixes, updates or support. Back up your data regularly.

The learning content has been prepared with care but does not replace official material (e.g.
curricula, exam catalogues). No warranty is given for its accuracy, completeness or currency, or for
exam results. The learning platform is not an offering of the German Chambers of Industry and
Commerce (IHK) and is not affiliated with them.

6. Final provisions

These terms are governed by German law. Mandatory consumer protection provisions of the country of
your habitual residence remain unaffected. If a provision is invalid, the remaining provisions
remain valid. Contact (e.g. for consent under section 3): https://github.com/Lemm1988
